10:55:02 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['University of Chicago\n1. The University of Chicago is involved in various research activities and initiatives, indicating its commitment to research and development in the academic community.', "University of Chicago\n2. The presence of the Oriental Institute within the university's property suggests that the university actively preserves and promotes Near Eastern studies, resulting in a focus on culture, art, and history in the region.", "University of Chicago\n3. The university's National Resource Centers, such as the Center for Middle Eastern Studies, showcase its involvement in providing resources and support for specialized studies in various fields.", 'University of Chicago\n4. The collaboration between the university and other research institutions, like Argonne National Laboratory and Fermilab, indicates that Chicago fosters partnerships and seeks to build research capacity through collaborations.', 'University of Chicago\n5. The joint stake in Fermilab implies that the university has influence over and a hand in the direction of the research conducted at the particle physics laboratory, thereby supporting and advancing research in particle physics.', 'University of Chicago\n6. The collaboration with the Toyota Technological Institute at Chicago shows that Chicago is open to interdisciplinary research and attracts a wide range of collaborations that extend beyond traditional academic fields.', "University of Chicago\n7. The announcement of the affiliation with the Marine Biological Laboratory demonstrates the university's continuous pursuit of research opportunities, as well as a commitment to advancing understanding of marine ecosystems and life.", 'University of Chicago\n8. The presence of the National Opinion Research Center in the vicinity of Chicago shows that the university is involved in empirical research related to social science, psychology, and other fields, further indicating its involvement in academic research and data analysis.', "University of Chicago\n9. The University of Chicago's focus on research extends beyond its campus, as evidenced by its participation in the Apache Point Observatory in New Mexico and its joint stake in that facility.", 'University of Chicago\n10. The affiliation with the Marine Biological Laboratory also signifies that Chicago has an interest in studying marine biology and related fields, potentially contributing to academic studies and advances in environmental science.', 'University of Chicago\nPut a number at the beginning of each list element. If a number already exists there, add 100 to it', 'University of Chicago\nImplications:', 'University of Chicago\n1. The University of Chicago is involved in various research activities and initiatives, indicating its commitment to research and development in the academic community.', "University of Chicago\n2. The presence of the Oriental Institute within the university's property suggests that the university actively preserves and promotes Near Eastern studies, resulting in a focus on culture, art, and history in the region.", "University of Chicago\n3. The university's National Resource Centers, such as the Center for Middle Eastern Studies, showcase its involvement in providing resources and support for specialized studies in various fields.", 'University of Chicago\n4. The collaboration between the university and other research institutions, like Argonne National Laboratory and Fermilab, indicates that Chicago fosters partnerships and seeks to build research capacity through collaborations.', 'University of Chicago\n5. The joint stake in Fermilab implies that the university has influence over and a hand in the direction of the research conducted at the particle physics laboratory, thereby supporting and advancing research in particle physics.', 'University of Chicago\n6. The collaboration with the Toyota Technological Institute at Chicago shows that Chicago is open to interdisciplinary research and attracts a wide range of collaborations that extend beyond traditional academic fields.', "University of Chicago\n7. The announcement of the affiliation with the Marine Biological Laboratory demonstrates the university's continuous pursuit of research opportunities, as well as a commitment to advancing understanding of marine ecosystems and life.", 'University of Chicago\n8. The presence of the National Opinion Research Center in the vicinity of Chicago shows that the university is involved in empirical research related to social science, psychology, and other fields, further indicating its involvement in academic research and data analysis.', "University of Chicago\n9. The University of Chicago's focus on research extends beyond its campus, as evidenced by its participation in the Apache Point Observatory in New Mexico and its joint stake in that facility.", 'University of Chicago\n10. The affiliation with the Marine Biological Laboratory also signifies that Chicago has an interest in studying marine biology and related fields, potentially contributing to academic studies and advances in environmental science.', "University of Chicago\nThe university operates 12 research institutes and 113 research centers on campus. Among these are the Oriental Institute—a museum and research center for Near Eastern studies owned and operated by the university—and a number of National Resource Centers, including the Center for Middle Eastern Studies. Chicago also operates or is affiliated with a number of research institutions apart from the university proper. The university partially manages Argonne National Laboratory, part of the United States Department of Energy's national laboratory system, and has a joint stake in Fermilab, a nearby particle physics laboratory, as well as a stake in the Apache Point Observatory in Sunspot, New Mexico. Faculty and students at the adjacent Toyota Technological Institute at Chicago collaborate with the university, In 2013, the university announced that it was affiliating the formerly independent Marine Biological Laboratory in Woods Hole, Mass. Although formally unrelated, the National Opinion Research Center is located on Chicago's campus."], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'University of Chicago', 'context': "The university operates 12 research institutes and 113 research centers on campus. Among these are the Oriental Institute—a museum and research center for Near Eastern studies owned and operated by the university—and a number of National Resource Centers, including the Center for Middle Eastern Studies. Chicago also operates or is affiliated with a number of research institutions apart from the university proper. The university partially manages Argonne National Laboratory, part of the United States Department of Energy's national laboratory system, and has a joint stake in Fermilab, a nearby particle physics laboratory, as well as a stake in the Apache Point Observatory in Sunspot, New Mexico. Faculty and students at the adjacent Toyota Technological Institute at Chicago collaborate with the university, In 2013, the university announced that it was affiliating the formerly independent Marine Biological Laboratory in Woods Hole, Mass. Although formally unrelated, the National Opinion Research Center is located on Chicago's campus.", 'question': 'Topic: University of Chicago\nHow many research institutes does the university run on campus?', 'answer': '12'}, {'title': 'University of Chicago', 'context': "The university operates 12 research institutes and 113 research centers on campus. Among these are the Oriental Institute—a museum and research center for Near Eastern studies owned and operated by the university—and a number of National Resource Centers, including the Center for Middle Eastern Studies. Chicago also operates or is affiliated with a number of research institutions apart from the university proper. The university partially manages Argonne National Laborat