11:04:48 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['Nikola Tesla\n1. Nikola Tesla had a significant amount of belongings, suggesting he may have been wealthy or well-known.', "Nikola Tesla\n2. His nephew, Sava Kosanović, felt compelled to protect Tesla's estate, indicating that it had value or significance.", "Nikola Tesla\n3. Kosanović's actions suggest that Tesla's work and/or personality may have been influential.", "Nikola Tesla\n4. The extensive shipping and display of Tesla's ashes in Belgrade indicate a high regard for his legacy or contribution to society.", 'Nikola Tesla\n5. Tesla\'s ashes being displayed alongside a "marble pedestal" suggests that he is viewed as a legendary figure or highly respected individual.', "Nikola Tesla\n6. The transfer of Tesla's estate occurred a few years after his death in 1952, indicating that he was still respected in his lifetime.", 'Nikola Tesla\n7. The ashes being "gold-plated" implies that Tesla was perceived as a valuable or extraordinary individual.', "Nikola Tesla\n8. The fact that his nephew made efforts to preserve Tesla's estate and legacy highlights the importance that his family placed on his work and influence.", "Nikola Tesla\n9. The museum in Belgrade displaying Tesla's ashes suggests that he has inspired other people and generations to appreciate his work.", "Nikola Tesla\n10. The transfer and exhibition of Tesla's estate and ashes occurred in 1952, 1957, and possibly later, which shows that there was at least some level of interest in honoring his legacy.", "Nikola Tesla\nLet's read the following passage and produce a list of implications derived directly or indirectly from the content.", 'Nikola Tesla\nPassage:', 'Nikola Tesla\nNikola Tesla (Serbian Cyrillic: Никола Тесла;[a] July 10, 1856July 7, 1943) was a Serbian-American inventor, electrical engineer, mechanical engineer, and physicist. He is best known for his contributions to the design of the modern alternating current (AC) electricity supply system.', 'Nikola Tesla\nImplications:', 'Nikola Tesla\n1. Nikola Tesla was a prominent inventor and scientist with multiple fields of expertise.', 'Nikola Tesla\n2. He was born in July 1856 and died in July 1943.', 'Nikola Tesla\n3. Tesla was Serbian by origin, and later became American.', 'Nikola Tesla\n4. He is primarily recognized for his role in the development of the modern AC electric power system.', 'Nikola Tesla\n5. Tesla was influential in the field of electrical engineering and electrical engineering specifically.', 'Nikola Tesla\n6. His inventions and innovations contributed to the advancement of science and technology in the late 19th and early 20th centuries.', 'Nikola Tesla\n7. AC electric power systems are a fundamental aspect of modern society and Tesla played a significant role in their development.', "Nikola Tesla\n8. Tesla's work in electrical and mechanical engineering, as well as physics, indicates that he was a highly knowledgeable and experienced individual.", 'Nikola Tesla\n9. His work has had a lasting impact on the fields of electrical engineering and power systems.', "Nikola Tesla\n10. Tesla's accomplishments have earned him a place among the most important inventors and scientists in history.", "Nikola Tesla\nIn 1952, following pressure from Tesla's nephew, Sava Kosanović, Tesla's entire estate was shipped to Belgrade in 80 trunks marked N.T. In 1957, Kosanović's secretary Charlotte Muzar transported Tesla's ashes from the United States to Belgrade. The ashes are displayed in a gold-plated sphere on a marble pedestal in the Nikola Tesla Museum."], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Nikola Tesla', 'context': "In 1952, following pressure from Tesla's nephew, Sava Kosanović, Tesla's entire estate was shipped to Belgrade in 80 trunks marked N.T. In 1957, Kosanović's secretary Charlotte Muzar transported Tesla's ashes from the United States to Belgrade. The ashes are displayed in a gold-plated sphere on a marble pedestal in the Nikola Tesla Mu