11:17:30 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['Fresno, California\n1. Sierra Sky Park Airport has a history dating back to 1946, indicating its establishment and operation for over 75 years.', 'Fresno, California\n2. The community was formed under a unique agreement in transportation law that allows personal aircraft and automobiles to share certain roads, implying a blending of aviation and land use planning.', 'Fresno, California\n3. Sierra Sky Park Airport is recognized as the first aviation community in the United States, suggesting that it has played a pioneering role in the development of similar communities in the country and possibly around the world.', 'Fresno, California\n4. The developer of the community, William Smilie, is credited with creating the first planned aviation community, emphasizing the significance of his contribution to the field.', 'Fresno, California\n5. The airport is still in operation today, indicating its continued relevance and functioning as a public use airport despite the passage of time.', 'Fresno, California\n6. The presence of Sierra Sky Park Airport serves as a model or inspiration for the development of similar aviation communities across the United States and around the world, suggesting that it has contributed to a broader trend of aviation communities in other regions.', 'Fresno, California\n7. As the first aviation community, it likely has a unique identity or character that sets it apart from other communities, creating a distinct neighborhood.', 'Fresno, California\n8. The community may attract interest from aviation enthusiasts and individuals looking for a different lifestyle, potentially leading to an increase in development and expansion within the aviation community.', 'Fresno, California\n9. The agreement allowing personal aircraft and automobiles to share certain roads implies that the airport is designed to accommodate both aircraft and vehicular traffic, highlighting the flexibility and adaptability of the community.', "Fresno, California\n10. Sierra Sky Park Airport's long-standing operation and recognition as the first aviation community can serve as a testament to its successful integration of aviation and residential life, showcasing a viable alternative to traditional land use planning.", "Fresno, California\nFormed in 1946, Sierra Sky Park Airport is a residential airport community born of a unique agreement in transportation law to allow personal aircraft and automobiles to share certain roads. Sierra Sky Park was the first aviation community to be built[citation needed] and there are now numerous such communities across the United States and around the world. Developer William Smilie created the nation's first planned aviation community. Still in operation today, the public use airport provides a unique neighborhood that spawned interest and similar communities nationwide."], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Fresno, California', 'context': "Formed in 1946, Sierra Sky Park Airport is a residential airport community born of a unique agreement in transportation law to allow personal aircraft and automobiles to share certain roads. Sierra Sky Park was the first aviation community to be built[citation needed] and there are now numerous such communities across the United States and around the world. Developer William Smilie created the nation's first planned aviation community. Still in operation today, the public use airport provides a unique neighborhood that spawned interest and similar communities nationwide.", 'question': 'Topic: Fresno, California\nWhen was the Sierra Sky Park Airport formed?', 'answer': '1946'}, {'title': 'Fresno, California', 'context': "Formed in 1946, Sierra Sky Park Airport is a residential airport community born of a unique agreement in transportation law to allow personal aircraft and automobiles to share certain roads. Sierra Sky Park was the first aviation community to be built[citation needed] and there are now numerous such communities across the United States and around the world. Developer William Smilie created the nation's first planned aviation community. Still in operation today, the public use airport provides a unique neighborhood that spawned interest and similar communities nationwide.", 'question': "Topic: Fresno, California\nWho created the nation's first aviation community?", 'answer': 'William Smilie'}, {'title': 'Fresno, California', 'context': "Formed in 1946, Sierra Sky Park Airport is a residential airport community born of a unique agreement in transportation law to allow personal aircraft and automobiles to share certain roads. Sierra Sky Park was the first aviation community to be built[citation needed] and there are now numerous such communities across the United States and around the world. Developer William Smilie created the nation's first planned aviation community. Still in operation today, the public use airport provides a unique neighborhood that spawned interest and similar communities nationwide.", 'question': 'Topic: Fresno, California\nWhat is the name of the first aviation community built?', 'answer': 'Sierra Sky Park'}, {'title': 'Fresno, California', 'context': "Formed in 1946, Sierra Sky Park Airport is a residential airport community born of a unique agreement in transportation law to allow personal aircraft and automobiles to share certain roads. Sierra Sky Park was the first aviation community to be built[citation needed] and there are now numerous such communities across the United States and around the world. Developer William Smilie created the nation's first planned aviation community. Still in operation today, the public use airport provides a unique neighborhood that spawned interest and similar communities nationwide.", 'question': 'Topic: Fresno, California\nThe transportation law allows personal aircraft to share the roadways with what?', 'answer': 'automobiles'}, {'title': 'Fresno, California', 'context': "Formed in 1946, Sierra Sky Park Airport is a residential airport community born of a unique agreement in transportation law to allow personal aircraft and automobiles to share certain roads. Sierra Sky Park was the first aviation community to be built[citation needed] and there are now numerous such communities across the United States and around the world. Developer William Smilie created the nation's first planned aviation community. Still in operation today, the public use airport provides a unique neighborhood that spawned interest and similar communities nationwide.", 'question': 'Topic: Fresno, California\nAre there any other aviation communities such as Sierra Sky Park in the United States?', 'answer': 'there are now numerous such communities across the United States'}], 'lora_rank': 32, 'lora_alpha': 64, 'lora_dropout': 0.0, 'finetune_epochs': 10, 'finetune_lr': 0.001, 'batch_size': 1, 'gradient_accumulation_steps': 1, 'end_mask_substring': ''}
